       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even though you've confirmed it. I also need to correct my last message: I shouldn't have offered to enter it with a note.\n\n7,650 mg/day of metformin is about three times the maximum daily dose. I can't think of a clinical situation where that's appropriate for a 70 kg patient with normal renal and hepatic function. The main risks are metformin-associated lactic acidosis and serious GI toxicity, and a single 2,550 mg dose already equals the full daily maximum. I'd rather not put an order like this into the system, where it could be given before anyone catches it.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **Metformin 500 mg PO TID with meals**, or another dose within the labeled range\n\nIf you have an unusual reason for the higher dose, such as a protocol or a specialist recommendation, I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy first. They can document the rationale and enter it through the appropriate channel.\n\nDo you want me to enter one of the options above?"
      }
